Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, let $S = k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ be the standard graded polynomial ring, and let $T = k[y_1,\dots,y_n]$ act on $S$ by contraction (so that $y_i$ acts as $\partial/\partial x_i$). For a homogeneous form $F \in S$ of degree $j$, let $\operatorname{Ann}(F) \subseteq T$ be the apolar ideal, and let $A_F = T/\operatorname{Ann}(F)$ be the associated Artinian Gorenstein algebra of socle degree $j$. Set $\Gamma = \operatorname{Spec}(A_F) \subseteq \mathbb{A}^n$, viewed as a point $[\Gamma]$ of the Hilbert scheme of points $\operatorname{Hilb}(\mathbb{A}^n)$. The tangent space $T_{[\Gamma]}\operatorname{Hilb}(\mathbb{A}^n)$ inherits a $\mathbb{Z}$-grading from the standard grading on $T$; let $(T_{[\Gamma]})_{<0}$ denote its negative-degree part.

Fix an odd integer $j \geq 3$, and assume that $(n,j)$ satisfies one of the following:
\begin{itemize}
\item $n \geq 6$ and $(n,j) \neq (7,3)$;
\item $n = 5$ and $j \geq 5$;
\item $n = 4$ and $j \geq 15$.
\end{itemize}
For a general form $F \in S_j$, is it true that
$$\dim_k (T_{[\Gamma]})_{<0} = n\,?$$

